toolong for Debian Bookworm
===========================

Bookworm's python3-textual (0.1.13) and python3-rich (13.3.1)
are older than toolong requires.
The source package therefore has two component tarballs,
`orig-textual` and `orig-rich`,
which dpkg-source unpacks into `textual/` and `rich/`.
debian/rules installs them together with toolong into /usr/share/toolong,
and /usr/bin/tl puts that directory first on `sys.path`.

`debian/build-source-package [OUTPUT_DIR]` builds the source package
from `debian/` in the working tree, the upstream source at `git HEAD`,
and the textual and rich sdists on PyPI.
Commit changes outside `debian/` first: `git archive` ignores the working tree.
Build the binary package from the resulting `.dsc`
with sbuild, or with `dpkg-source -x` and `dpkg-buildpackage`.
